WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.830
As lengthy as the run time was for Avengers:
Infinity War, there's still more of the movie

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.970
we didn't see, and directors Joe and Anthony
Russo have indicated that fans can expect

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.290
plenty of bonus material to come in the take-home
copies of the film.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.960
Although they've yet to spell out exactly
which deleted and extended scenes could be

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.199
included, they, along with the film's cast,
have shared a few hints about what might be

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:22.310
missing from the movie's theatrical version.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:26.669
Here's a look at some of the Avengers: Infinity
War scenes that might make the DVD extras,

00:00:26.669 --> 00:00:29.590
and a few that may never see the light of
day.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.560
Guardians get silly

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.660
One missing scene the Russo brothers have
promised involves the Guardians of the Galaxy

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.480
flexing their funny bones.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.270
Anthony Russo told Entertainment Weekly:

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.640
"It's a scene where they're sort of stuck.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.170
There's a point in the movie where they're
stuck without knowing what to do.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:48.300
… it was really fun and it was very endearing
to us.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:53.370
But because the movie is so big and so propulsive,
it just wasn't quite pushing us where we needed

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.370
to go."

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:58.960
That description indicates this is an extension
of the scene on Knowhere when Peter Quill,

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:04.510
Drax, and Mantis are duped by Thanos' reality
stone trickery and left to fester on the broken

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:05.510
planet.

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:09.310
Russo confirmed as much in a later interview
with ComicBook.com, saying:

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:13.509
"It's at that moment in the movie where they
have lost Gamora to Thanos in the Knowhere

00:01:13.509 --> 00:01:15.119
and they don't know what to do about it.

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:16.270
They don't know where to go.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.940
They have no idea what to do.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.819
And it serves as this very absurd scene about
the Guardians not knowing what to do, that's

00:01:22.819 --> 00:01:24.039
very, very funny."

00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:28.840
In other words, expect to see some more humor
from the Star-Lord that might help make fans

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.080
less mad at him.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.080
"Wow."

00:01:31.569 --> 00:01:33.060
Pepper &amp; Co. in the park

00:01:33.069 --> 00:01:37.150
In one of the earliest scenes from Infinity
War, Tony Stark can be seen taking a walk

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:41.789
with his lady love Pepper Potts as the two
discuss his dream about her being pregnant

00:01:41.789 --> 00:01:44.700
before he runs off to deal with Thanos' looming
threat.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.970
That exchange may have been a mere primer
for what's still to come between the two in

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:52.310
Avengers 4, but it was also an abbreviated
version of what was actually filmed.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:57.009
Screenplay co-writer Christopher Markus told
GameSpot that there were a lot more people

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:59.100
who joined the fray for that scene, saying:

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:04.470
"We shot an unbelievably long version of Tony
and Pepper in the park that features cameos.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.170
It was sort of Robert and his friends' day
at the park."

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:11.500
Judging from behind-the-scenes footage taken
during the shoot, Happy may be one of the

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.099
missing persons we can expect to see in the
fuller version.

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:16.810
"Go team, yeahhhh."

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.670
Hulkbuster smash?

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:21.930
Much has been made of the fact that Bruce
Banner was unable to transform into the Hulk

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.090
on cue in Avengers: Infinity War.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.060
But there may be reason to believe another
version of the film might've featured Hulk

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.110
going berserk in the Hulkbuster suit.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:34.590
While we know that the trailer's big tracking
shot was made specifically to mislead audiences

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:39.129
about what was to come on the Banner-Hulk
front in the Battle of Wakanda, there are

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:43.270
other glimpses from the trailer that seem
to indicate some Hulk smashing as well.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:47.090
For example, there's a moment in the first
trailer when Bruce is shown standing next

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:51.000
to a broken version of the Hulkbuster suit,
looking a little embarrassed.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.500
Although there's no official indication that
a Hulk in the Hulkbuster suit scene was shot,

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.750
the fact that Funko Pop released a toy version
of the green giant breaking through the red

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.780
get-up has led some fans to believe it points
to yet another scene that didn't make the

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:07.140
final cut of the film but might find its way
into your home copy.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.000
Now, let's talk about a few of those scenes
that were thought up but never produced...

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.769
A Civil War reunion

00:03:13.769 --> 00:03:18.510
Perhaps the most disappointing aspect of Avengers:
Infinity War is that it didn't fully resolve

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.290
the conflict between Iron Man and Captain
America.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:25.740
Sure, there's a detente between the two that
comes by way of flip phone, but the two don't

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.629
share the screen, even though they're fighting
for the same team again.

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:33.459
According to co-writer Stephen McFeely, however,
at least one draft of the film's script would've

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:35.420
brought them back together at last.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.689
He told Yahoo Movies:

00:03:36.689 --> 00:03:41.049
"Our first sort of wonky draft [featured]
the idea that they had to get back in the

00:03:41.049 --> 00:03:42.310
same room together.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:45.550
That meant that you're slowing down your Thanos
Stones plot to deal with other threads from

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:46.550
other movies.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:50.549
As much as we wanted to do it, and as many
times as we wrote those scenes, [it] became

00:03:50.549 --> 00:03:54.650
clear that this movie needed to be propulsive
and be about Thanos and what he represented

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:55.819
to the Avengers."

00:03:55.819 --> 00:04:00.140
It's not over yet, however, and Joe Russo
has teased that Captain America: Civil War

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:03.519
contains a big hint about what's to come in
Avengers 4.

00:04:03.519 --> 00:04:08.019
So, now that Iron Man has been left alone
on Titan, perhaps the next film will finally

00:04:08.019 --> 00:04:10.900
bring their face-to-face scene to fruition.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.370
"Let's go."

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.019
The power stone

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:19.109
While Avengers: Infinity War showed how Thanos
acquired most of the Infinity Stones, we didn't

00:04:19.109 --> 00:04:23.810
get to see him claim the Power Stone, which
had previously been left in the care of the

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.690
Nova Corps on Xandar.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:29.840
According to McFeely, the scene was originally
written into the film, but had to be edited

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:32.610
out of the working script for the sake of
streamlining the story.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:34.220
As he explained to Yahoo!

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.220
Movies:

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.680
"I do remember, there was a Xandar draft,
and it just became unwieldy.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:43.030
It's lovely to go back to a small part of
Guardians of the Galaxy and explore how you

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:46.389
get that stone, but we had to eventually economize."

00:04:46.389 --> 00:04:51.070
So instead of seeing the Mad Titan destroy
that planet, we only get to hear about it

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.070
secondhand.

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:56.400
Similarly, fans also never get to find out
exactly how he snagged the Reality Stone,

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.060
because the Guardians don't arrive until after
he's collected the Aether from the Collector.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:03.360
The next chapter

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:08.350
Since Avengers: Infinity War and Avengers
4 are two parts of one overarching narrative,

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:12.699
there was bound to be at least a little confusion
over which scenes were filmed for which movies,

00:05:12.699 --> 00:05:15.940
and some of the cast's interviews reflect
as much … or do they?

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:20.509
There have been several instances of Avengers
stars discussing production on scenes that

00:05:20.509 --> 00:05:21.509
we haven't seen yet.

00:05:21.509 --> 00:05:26.940
"Did you thrust your hand towards someone
wearing like a blue suit with ping pong glued

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:27.940
on."

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:28.940
"Yes."

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:30.750
"Then you still have powers."

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:34.940
One of the biggest points of confusion seems
to center around whether a giant group scene

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:37.960
would be included in Infinity War or the next
film.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.970
"In one particular scene there's like 32 of
us.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:41.970
There's a lot.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:46.539
There's so many of us I don't even know who's
a Marvel character and who's a crew member."

00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:51.360
Mark Ruffalo implied he'd worked with Tilda
Swinton and Cate Blanchett, which made folks

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:55.039
believe the Ancient One and the Goddess of
Death would make an appearance at some point.

00:05:55.039 --> 00:05:59.640
And Sebastian Stan said it included everyone
from Nick Fury to Janet Van Dyne.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:03.490
Even the Russos seemed to be confused about
where it'd end up; they agreed there'd be

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:08.360
a Civil War airport-sized scene in Infinity
War, with Joe Russo saying:

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:12.509
"We have like an equivalent that's like, you
know if you had a comic book and you open

00:06:12.509 --> 00:06:15.389
it up to your double panel and then you fold
it out.

00:06:15.389 --> 00:06:17.509
And then you folded it out again and again."

00:06:17.509 --> 00:06:21.940
Since nothing like that came through in Infinity
War, we just have to believe it's being reserved

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.599
for round four instead.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:26.270
But we'll have to wait 'til next year to find
out for sure.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:27.700
"Boom."

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.740
Thanks for watching!

00:06:28.759 --> 00:06:31.199
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:31.199 --> 00:06:33.460
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

